(text "R8-R26: 220 ohm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 358.14 223.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "ef7ff226-4a29-482a-b036-00bc2da1f743"))
(text "Skeet Shoot 8088 computer on one sheet. Every connection is a drawn wire; the address and data buses are continuous bus lines across the middle (A[0..19], D[0..7]), each chip joining\nthrough bus entries (labels name the members). Top: clock, 8088, latches and buffers, 8253 timer + speaker, 8259 interrupts. Bottom: I/O decode, 8255, LED bar, display, switches; memory.\nCLOCK AND RESET (8284A, 12 MHz crystal, RC reset) ARE RECONSTRUCTED (2026): not in the 2007 drawings. IC power pins are implied (VCC/GND) as on the printed figures.\nIncludes the 2026 corrections listed on each figure sheet and in README.txt (wiring that differs from the 2007 printout)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 69.85 24.13 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid "5a397686-6c94-4b4c-ba77-e045590147d1"))
